            <ArticleTitle>[Tiapride : a clinical study in a department of internal medicine (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2024-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Effectiveness and tolerance of tiapride were studied in twenty patients in a department of internal medicine. Tiapride was effective against acute manifestations of alcoholism and against agitation, especially in the elderly. There were no serious side-effects, particularly on hemodynamics and vigilance. At the dosage used in our study the analgesic effect of tiapride was both unreliable and transient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
